<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shahaji Bhonsle</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1594">1594</a>–<a href="/years/1664">1664</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Shahaji</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shahaji Bhonsle was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> general in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> and father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a>, founder of the Maratha kingdom. He served the Ahmadnagar Sultanate and, after its fall to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a>, briefly propped up a puppet Nizam Shah until he surrendered in 1636. He then entered the service of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adil-shahi-dynasty">Bijapur Sultanate</a>, holding estates around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pune">Pune</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengaluru">Bangalore</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shahaji-bhonsle.jpg" alt="Shahaji Bhonsle" width="320" height="495" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: अज्ञात · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shahajiraje_Bhosale.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
